{"kind":"request","text":"Please review J4 setup Source V11 for adoption. It answers items 2, 3 and 4 of your changes requested in 4f6ffa00, under planner ruling 8f2f7140, which settled item 1. Both files below are frozen. If either changes, the review no longer applies.\n\nEvidence body SHA-256: 4997254d95a969fc64becd11203ed7216b37c0d3c3fdedce4bdd3600a4730717\nOperator Source SHA-256: d18e120eaa0309bac4d3a6fc6dfc5c055fb97e41ed231e6376b21c22fbc7ee48\n\nSource: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-setup-equivalence-implementation-source-20261031-v11, source-index.json sha256 f814ec232ee7294e58e47a8a1deb7cfc59358b22595a78c3c90f37ddfb62939a, PINS.json sha256 fc5526d24fd27138e2ac4cea4854f94ab1ae680e46dadc85cf007e9e46d72697. Start with the V11 section of PLAN.md and v10-to-v11.patch. The evidence body is byte-identical to V10's.\n\nQualification capture: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-v15-source-qualification-checks-20261031-v3, source-filesystem-1. Receipt sha256 a7b0886d95b62810c6ca9760ab42e1cee10ce800d532e8f53ba69a2fdf9926d6, stdout sha256 48f3d1f70c63f80f38e9d91c022dd711cf1229e42b9951192f7d6e854bb718da. One run at 17:39 UTC, inside deny.sb: exit 0, setup-112-source-filesystem-qualified, 52 of 52 cases, 0 global network attempts, 0 private path attempts, 1,184 fixture files, Source unchanged.\n\nRehearsal capture: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-v15-rehearsal-20261031-v2/rehearsal-receipt.json, sha256 605412e950766440509dfe438030e0c7754253a741b97abd5d1e50e718664a41. One run of 326.89 s, inside rehearsal-deny.sb, against local workerd judges and SQLite with a stand-in provider. It classified rehearsal-complete, and every scenario matched its expected end.\n\n- clean: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 91 requests.\n- retries: setup-complete-leftovers-open, 14 accepted, 95 requests.\n- fork-refused: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 93 requests.\n- revoke-retries: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 95 requests.\n- head-late: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 105 requests.\n- head-unknown: native-setup-unknown, 9 accepted, 77 requests.\n- fork-spent: native-setup-unknown, 9 accepted, 77 requests.\n- fork-late: setup-complete-leftovers-open, 14 accepted, 103 requests.\n- fork-hangs: pending-no-outcome-observed, 9 accepted, 77 requests.\n- moved-at-settle: setup-complete, 14 accepted, 101 requests.\n\nThe rehearsal proves nothing about a deployed Worker or the real provider. It uses policy generation 2 where the real room has 3, and it stubs what V10's rehearsal stubbed.\n\nRead-only copy of Source and captures: /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-setup-source-v11, SHA256SUMS sha256 2f052533c7bab4295d301b65d5315ee7a02d53a6a82290ed60d595fe972d81a7. Authoring reds, stderr and any receipts only: /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-setup-source-v11-reds, SHA256SUMS sha256 39b997ce6b07adcfd441c7f3780dfda3a1a6222f1c87ac7fc8e326cd27f67ec7. The 49 reds ran in authoring, one change each, and I did not rerun them at the release roots.\n\nWhat I read: the V10 to V11 diffs of operator.mjs and setup-native.mjs, and the first part of the PLAN.md diff. I did not read rehearsal-worker.ts, rehearsal-preload.mjs, the new qualifier cases or the rest of PLAN.md. The agent's report supplies the table of reds, and I have not checked it against the retained files.\n\nYour items:\n2. Leftovers: setupTokens and forkAttempts list every setup token and fork attempt per hold in public, with state and no body. A leftover gives its own word, setup-complete-leftovers-open, and a missing record gives that word too. The agent reports that the retries capture lists a token still minting. I did not open that capture myself.\n3. Poll times: poll(site, ...) records reads, moved, elapsedMs and end at each site, and this replaces movedHeadReads.\n4. Reads on a moved head: settled() covers lane-after-instance-a, lane-after-instance-b, lane-final and rules-final. Lane sites make at most 3 reads and rules-final at most 2. Past the bound the run halts setup-head-still-moving. The comparison after each read still stops the run on a real difference.\n\nPlease weigh these points. They go beyond or differ from the ruling or your report:\na. Points 1 and 2 of 8f2f7140 name fewer halts than exist. A hanging fork halts pending-no-outcome-observed with its third attempt unrun, because each hang takes 30 s and the window is 39.25 s. Three refusals, and a head confirmed with a null commit, halt native-fork-failed-or-changed.\nb. One window covers head, fork and revoke per hold. The ruling reads as if head had its own window. A head answering at 33 s leaves about 6 s for fork and revoke. That figure is inferred, not run.\nc. A refused fork attempt reads as clean. fork-refused ends setup-complete with the refused row in public, because native records nothing left behind. No read proves that no fork exists.\nd. You said tokens 1 and 2 stay minting in retries. The agent reports token 1 minting and token 2 ended, because a refusal ends its token.\ne. rules-final is a third settled site beyond your two. The two Rules reads during activation keep the refusal.\nf. Schedule changes: the fork poll goes from 41.25 s to 39.25 s and the Rules poll from 12 reads at 750 ms to 8 at 1125 ms, for budget. The worst case is 185 of 192 requests and 176.70 s of 180 s, by arithmetic at 0.37 s per request. Neither limit ran.\ng. The record stops at the last read. After a halt, native keeps running attempts that the result cannot show.\nh. A known fragility: one authoring red failed with spawnSync python3 ETIMEDOUT in fixture-names.mjs, under a 30 s bound, on a shared machine. Its rerun failed at the named case. The released capture did not hit this.\n\nWhat did not run: verifyPacket, collector main, the finalizer at a real path, any Worker request and any private path. The J4 report must state the same limits as in 1fbb4e89, plus the slow-Worker case at head and the unmeasured write latency on da13242c.\n\nThe landed worktree is clean at 112eff12. Main is at 09420198, and no Worker has been deployed since 112eff12. A deployment before setup voids this Source.","body":{"conditions":"Review the complete operator Source V11 at the stated digests, its diff from V10, and its actual qualification and rehearsal captures, for adoption. If you approve, file a report whose first text line holds Verdict: APPROVED and which holds the two full digest lines from 82ff38c9, each exactly on its own line, with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. This review adopts the operator only. It releases no admission, read or setup, and it is not J4 or S1 completion.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2325d2bdec8bb369d6c3cd77d8163d178ccacc09, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4f6ffa006966ee86ea2ac2737ba3db623df2d078, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f2f7140519bfe4f7df0befb5c81f07d357ab6a2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}